# Every content_hash in this project (docs/rubric.md, docs/analysis-plan.md, golden manifests,
# models.yaml) is a SHA-256 of raw file bytes, computed via Path.read_bytes(). Git's autocrlf
# can silently rewrite those bytes on checkout (CRLF on Windows, LF in CI on Ubuntu), producing a
# different hash for byte-identical content on different platforms -- which breaks freeze_rubric's
# "already frozen with a different hash" check and any downstream contamination/manifest proof.
# eol=lf pins line endings to LF everywhere, regardless of core.autocrlf, so the same commit
# always hashes the same way on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
